<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>About me — Laird Scabar</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Sport, the Terry Fox Run, small businesses, ten years on film sets, travelling, and the outdoors — the longer version of Laird Scabar."
    />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="format1.css" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />
    <script>
      document.documentElement.classList.add("js");
      if (localStorage.getItem("theme") === "dark") {
        document.documentElement.classList.add("pre-dark");
      }
    </script>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="topbar" id="topbar">
      <div class="shell topbar-inner">
        <a class="brand" href="index.html">
          <span class="brand-mark">LS</span>
          Laird Scabar
        </a>

        <button class="icon-btn nav-toggle" id="nav-toggle" type="button" aria-label="Toggle navigation" aria-expanded="false">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round">
            <line x1="4" y1="7" x2="20" y2="7" /><line x1="4" y1="12" x2="20" y2="12" /><line x1="4" y1="17" x2="20" y2="17" />
          </svg>
        </button>

        <nav class="topnav" id="topnav">
          <a href="index.html#skills">Skills</a>
          <a href="index.html#experience">Experience</a>
          <a href="index.html#projects">Projects</a>
          <a href="about.html" aria-current="page">About me</a>
          <a href="index.html#contact">Contact</a>
        </nav>

        <div class="topbar-actions">
          <button class="icon-btn theme-toggle" id="theme-toggle" type="button" aria-label="Toggle dark mode">
            <svg class="moon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <path d="M21 12.79A9 9 0 1 1 11.21 3 7 7 0 0 0 21 12.79z" />
            </svg>
            <svg class="sun" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4.5" />
              <path d="M12 2v2M12 20v2M4.9 4.9l1.4 1.4M17.7 17.7l1.4 1.4M2 12h2M20 12h2M4.9 19.1l1.4-1.4M17.7 6.3l1.4-1.4" />
            </svg>
          </button>
          <a class="btn btn--sm" href="assets/LairdsResume.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Resume</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main class="shell">
      <section class="page-head reveal">
        <span class="eyebrow">About me</span>
        <h1>Outside of school and engineering</h1>
        <p class="section-lede">
          I'm Laird — a mechanical and mechatronics engineering student at UBC.
          Before any of that I was a kid on a rink, on a court, and on film sets.
          All of it is still the reason I like building things.
        </p>

        <nav class="chapter-nav">
          <a href="#sports">Sports</a>
          <a href="#terryfox">Terry Fox</a>
          <a href="#business">Businesses</a>
          <a href="#acting">Acting</a>
          <a href="#travel">Travelling</a>
          <a href="#outdoors">Outdoors</a>
        </nav>
      </section>

      <!-- ===================== SPORTS ===================== -->
      <section class="life reveal" id="sports">
        <div class="life-head">
          <span class="eyebrow">01 — Sports</span>
          <h2>Thirteen years of showing up</h2>
          <p>
            I've played competitive sports my whole life — volleyball and hockey,
            multiple provincial banners, and <strong>silver at Volleyball
            Nationals in 2023</strong>. In October 2024 I was named BC School
            Sports Athlete of the Month for volleyball.
          </p>
          <p>
            What I actually took from it wasn't the medals. It was reps — showing
            up, getting it wrong in front of people, adjusting, and going again.
            That's the exact loop I run now on a CAD model or a prototype that
            won't behave.
          </p>
          <ul class="life-points">
            <li>BC School Sports Athlete of the Month — volleyball, October 2024</li>
            <li>Silver at Volleyball Nationals 2023, plus multiple provincial banners</li>
            <li>Captain of ice hockey, ball hockey, ultimate and volleyball at Fraser Heights</li>
            <li>Captain of my club volleyball team · PCAHA Scholarship Award recipient</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="mosaic" data-gallery="sports">
          <div class="photo p-big">
            <img src="assets/volleyball-athlete.jpg" alt="BC School Sports Athlete of the Month, October 2024" loading="lazy" />
            <span class="cap">BC Athlete of the Month — Oct '24</span>
          </div>
          <div class="photo">
            <img src="assets/hockey-awards.jpg" alt="PCAHA scholarship award presentation" loading="lazy" />
            <span class="cap">PCAHA Scholarship Award</span>
          </div>
          <div class="photo">
            <img src="assets/volleyball-team.jpg" alt="Volleyball team" loading="lazy" />
            <span class="cap">Club volleyball</span>
          </div>
          <div class="photo p-wide">
            <img src="assets/hockey-team.jpg" alt="Hockey team" loading="lazy" />
            <span class="cap">On the ice</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ===================== TERRY FOX ===================== -->
      <section class="life reveal" id="terryfox">
        <div class="life-head">
          <span class="eyebrow">02 — Terry Fox</span>
          <h2>Every year since 2020</h2>
          <p>
            Since 2020 I've helped organize volunteers and coordinate fundraisers
            for the annual Terry Fox Run in my community. It's the thing I'm
            proudest of that has nothing to do with engineering.
          </p>
          <p>
            I've gathered sponsors, recruited volunteers out of my high school,
            worked with government officials to plan the route, and run the merch
            and barbecue tables on race day. Collectively that work has
            contributed to <strong>over $50,000 raised for cancer
            research</strong>.
          </p>
          <ul class="life-points">
            <li>Organizing volunteers and fundraisers since 2020</li>
            <li>Recruited student volunteers and secured local sponsors</li>
            <li>Coordinated route planning with municipal officials</li>
            <li>Over $50,000 contributed to cancer research</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="mosaic" data-gallery="terryfox">
          <div class="photo p-big">
            <img src="assets/terryfox-run.jpg" alt="Terry Fox Run volunteer team" loading="lazy" />
            <span class="cap">Terry Fox Run 2025 — the volunteer crew</span>
          </div>
          <div class="photo">
            <img src="assets/terryfox-booth.jpg" alt="Terry Fox fundraising booth" loading="lazy" />
            <span class="cap">Fundraising booth</span>
          </div>
          <div class="photo">
            <img src="assets/terryfox-shirts.jpg" alt="Terry Fox run shirts" loading="lazy" />
            <span class="cap">Shirt sales</span>
          </div>
          <div class="photo p-wide">
            <img src="assets/terryfox-setup.jpg" alt="Setting up on race day" loading="lazy" />
            <span class="cap">Race day setup</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ===================== BUSINESSES ===================== -->
      <section class="life reveal" id="business">
        <div class="life-head">
          <span class="eyebrow">03 — Businesses</span>
          <h2>I keep starting things</h2>
          <p>
            I've started a few small businesses, mostly because I wanted to find
            out whether I could. A <strong>mobile auto detailing business</strong>
            — foam cannon, pressure washer, driveway visits on weekends — and a
            <strong>dropshipping store</strong> I built and scaled to roughly
            $4,500 a month while I was 16.
          </p>
          <p>
            Neither was going to change the world, but running them taught me
            pricing, customer service, ad spend, logistics, and how quickly a plan
            collapses when it meets a real customer. That's the same feeling as a
            first prototype, just with a different kind of feedback.
          </p>
          <ul class="life-points">
            <li>Mobile auto detailing — booking, pricing, and the actual work</li>
            <li>Dropshipping store scaled to roughly $4,500/month at 16</li>
            <li>Everything from ad creative to fulfilment and support</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="mosaic" data-gallery="business">
          <div class="photo p-big">
            <img src="assets/detailing.jpg" alt="Foam cannon detailing a car in a driveway" loading="lazy" />
            <span class="cap">Foam cannon, driveway, weekend</span>
          </div>
          <div class="photo">
            <img src="assets/detailing-2.jpg" alt="Detailing work" loading="lazy" />
            <span class="cap">Interior detail</span>
          </div>
          <div class="photo">
            <img src="assets/detailing-3.jpg" alt="Finished detail" loading="lazy" />
            <span class="cap">Finished</span>
          </div>
          <div class="photo p-wide">
            <img src="assets/dropship-store.png" alt="Dropshipping storefront" loading="lazy" />
            <span class="cap">The storefront</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ===================== ACTING ===================== -->
      <section class="life reveal" id="acting">
        <div class="life-head">
          <span class="eyebrow">04 — Acting</span>
          <h2>Ten years on set</h2>
          <p>
            I've been acting since I was eight years old. Over about a decade I
            worked on live-action and animated productions with
            <strong>Netflix, Disney, CBC, Amazon Prime</strong> and others.
          </p>
          <p>
            Film sets are the best crash course in professionalism you can get as
            a kid: hit your mark, know your material, take direction without ego,
            and be easy to work with when everyone is tired. That translated to
            team rooms and design reviews more directly than I expected. It's on
            pause while I'm at UBC.
          </p>
          <a class="text-link" href="https://www.imdb.com/name/nm9478122/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            See the IMDb page <span class="arrow">→</span>
          </a>
        </div>

        <div class="mosaic" data-gallery="acting">
          <div class="photo p-big">
            <img src="assets/acting-chair.jpg" alt="On set in a cast chair" loading="lazy" />
            <span class="cap">Between takes</span>
          </div>
          <div class="photo">
            <img src="assets/littleme.jpeg" alt="Laird as a young child" loading="lazy" />
            <span class="cap">Early days</span>
          </div>
          <div class="photo">
            <img src="assets/lilme.jpeg" alt="Laird as a child on the beach at Tofino" loading="lazy" />
            <span class="cap">Tofino, a long time ago</span>
          </div>
          <div class="photo p-wide">
            <img src="assets/acting-set.jpg" alt="On a production set" loading="lazy" />
            <span class="cap">On location</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ===================== TRAVELLING ===================== -->
      <section class="life reveal" id="travel">
        <div class="life-head">
          <span class="eyebrow">05 — Travelling</span>
          <h2>Going somewhere with a trail on it</h2>
          <p>
            Travelling is my favourite way to spend money. My favourite trip so
            far was <strong>hiking the Dolomites in Italy</strong> — long days,
            huge limestone walls, and the kind of scenery that doesn't
            photograph properly no matter how hard you try.
          </p>
          <p>
            I plan trips around what I can walk up. If a place has a ridgeline, a
            reef, or a mountain pass, that's usually enough of a reason to go.
          </p>
          <ul class="life-points">
            <li>The Dolomites, Italy — the standout so far</li>
            <li>Sea-to-Sky and the BC interior most summers</li>
            <li>Always looking for the next trail worth the flight</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="mosaic" data-gallery="travel">
          <div class="photo p-big">
            <img src="assets/italy.jpeg" alt="Hiking a misty alpine trail in the Dolomites" loading="lazy" />
            <span class="cap">The Dolomites, Italy</span>
          </div>
          <div class="photo">
            <img src="assets/travel-2.jpg" alt="Travel photo" loading="lazy" />
            <span class="cap">On the road</span>
          </div>
          <div class="photo">
            <img src="assets/travel-3.jpg" alt="Travel photo" loading="lazy" />
            <span class="cap">Somewhere good</span>
          </div>
          <div class="photo p-wide">
            <img src="assets/travel-4.jpg" alt="Travel photo" loading="lazy" />
            <span class="cap">Worth the flight</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ===================== OUTDOORS ===================== -->
      <section class="life reveal" id="outdoors">
        <div class="life-head">
          <span class="eyebrow">06 — Outdoors</span>
          <h2>Snowboarding, surfing, and everything between</h2>
          <p>
            When I'm not in a lab or a machine shop I'm usually on a mountain. I
            snowboard all winter, surf and paddle board on the coast, and hike
            whatever's in range the rest of the year.
          </p>
          <p>
            Living in BC makes this unreasonably easy — alpine sunrises an hour
            from campus, the coast for surfing, and local mountains that stay
            good until spring.
          </p>
          <ul class="life-points">
            <li>Snowboarding the local mountains all winter</li>
            <li>Surfing and paddle boarding on the coast</li>
            <li>Hiking the North Shore and Sea-to-Sky</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="mosaic" data-gallery="outdoors">
          <div class="photo p-big">
            <img src="assets/snowboard.jpeg" alt="Snowboarding at sunset above the clouds" loading="lazy" />
            <span class="cap">Sunset lap above the clouds</span>
          </div>
          <div class="photo">
            <img src="assets/surfing.jpeg" alt="Surfing" loading="lazy" />
            <span class="cap">Surfing the coast</span>
          </div>
          <div class="photo">
            <img src="assets/Me1.jpeg" alt="Coal Harbour seawall at night" loading="lazy" />
            <span class="cap">Coal Harbour</span>
          </div>
          <div class="photo p-wide">
            <img src="assets/hiking-lookout.jpg" alt="A lookout over the water" loading="lazy" />
            <span class="cap">The lookout</span>
          </div>
          <div class="photo p-wide">
            <img src="assets/Me2.jpeg" alt="Vancouver skyline at night" loading="lazy" />
            <span class="cap">Vancouver at night</span>
          </div>
          <div class="photo">
            <img src="assets/hiking-clouds.jpg" alt="Hiking above the clouds" loading="lazy" />
            <span class="cap">Above the clouds</span>
          </div>
          <div class="photo">
            <img src="assets/paddleboard.jpg" alt="Paddle boarding" loading="lazy" />
            <span class="cap">Paddle boarding</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ===================== CONTACT ===================== -->
      <section class="section" id="contact">
        <div class="section-head reveal">
          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">Contact</span>
            <h2 class="section-title">That's the whole story</h2>
            <p class="section-lede">
              If any of it resonated — or you just want to talk about
              engineering, sports, or something you're building — I'd love to
              hear from you.
            </p>
          </div>
          <a class="text-link" href="index.html#projects">Back to the projects <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
        </div>

        <div class="contact-grid reveal">
          <button class="contact-method" type="button" id="copy-email" data-email="lairdscabar@gmail.com">
            <span class="contact-method-icon">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <rect x="2.5" y="4.5" width="19" height="15" rx="2.5" /><path d="m3 7 9 6 9-6" />
              </svg>
            </span>
            <h3>Email</h3>
            <p>Best for internships, co-op roles, or anything you want to build.</p>
            <span class="contact-method-detail">lairdscabar@gmail.com</span>
            <span class="contact-method-action" id="copy-state">Click to copy</span>
          </button>

          <a class="contact-method" href="https://linkedin.com/in/lairdscabar" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            <span class="contact-method-icon">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M4.98 3.5a2.5 2.5 0 1 1 0 5 2.5 2.5 0 0 1 0-5zM3 9h4v12H3zM9 9h3.8v1.7h.05c.53-1 1.83-2.05 3.77-2.05 4.03 0 4.78 2.65 4.78 6.1V21h-4v-5.4c0-1.29-.02-2.95-1.8-2.95-1.8 0-2.07 1.4-2.07 2.85V21H9z" /></svg>
            </span>
            <h3>LinkedIn</h3>
            <p>Best for staying connected and seeing what I'm working on.</p>
            <span class="contact-method-detail">linkedin.com/in/lairdscabar</span>
            <span class="contact-method-action">Open profile →</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

